<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  fastdds_udp.xml — SHM-disabled UDPv4 profile
  ============================================================
  Used by containers that must NOT actively peer with Isaac Sim
  (robot_description, lidar, navigation, rviz).

  Why not fastdds_sim.xml here:
    Isaac Sim (10.42.101.217) exposes ~20 DDS participants. Any container in
    its initialPeersList gets flooded with EDP announcements for all of them,
    throttling ROS callbacks to ~12%.  fastdds_sim.xml is reserved for
    containers that actively bridge to Isaac Sim (joy, teleop, slam_manager)
    and for rf2o_lidar (which needs to receive /tf_static RELIABLE/TRANSIENT_LOCAL
    from robot_description — see docker-compose.sim.yaml rf2o_lidar comment).

  What this profile does:
    useBuiltinTransports: false — excludes the SHM transport and the builtin UDP
    userTransports: [udpv4]     — adds a plain custom UDPv4 as the only transport

  Why custom UDPv4 instead of builtin UDP:
    The builtin UDPv4 and the SHM transport are registered as a pair when
    useBuiltinTransports is true.  There is no FastDDS XML knob to keep
    builtin UDP while removing only SHM (FASTDDS_BUILTIN_TRANSPORTS=UDPv4 env
    var exists in FastDDS ≥2.9 but is not available on all Pi builds).
    A custom UDPv4 transport (type:UDPv4, no extra fields) reproduces the
    builtin UDP port-formula behaviour — PDP/EDP/data ports are identical —
    so same-profile containers communicate correctly.

  Cross-profile communication (this profile ↔ fastdds_sim.xml):
    Both profiles use the same custom UDPv4 type with the same port formulas.
    fastdds_sim.xml containers (teleop, etc.) do communicate with fastdds_udp.xml
    containers (navigation, etc.) for RELIABLE topics such as /cmd_vel_nav. Any
    container that must exchange RELIABLE/TRANSIENT_LOCAL topics (e.g. /tf_static)
    with these containers must use either this profile or fastdds_sim.xml.
    A default-DDS (empty profile, SHM+builtin-UDP) container may receive
    BEST_EFFORT topics from here but RELIABLE/TRANSIENT_LOCAL exchange fails due
    to mismatched unicast port locators.
-->
<profiles xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
  <transport_descriptors>
    <transport_descriptor>
      <transport_id>udpv4</transport_id>
      <type>UDPv4</type>
    </transport_descriptor>
  </transport_descriptors>

  <participant profile_name="participant_profile" is_default_profile="true">
    <rtps>
      <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      <userTransports>
        <transport_id>udpv4</transport_id>
      </userTransports>
    </rtps>
  </participant>
</profiles>
